      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Quesada names 33-man squad as 15 Italy players miss Springboks Test",
          "body": "Italy have confirmed 15 key men are unavailable through injury for the Turin Test against South Africa, including captain Michele Lamaro and Tommaso Menoncello, with Ignacio Brex and Sebastian Negri also out. Tighthead Marco Riccioni is unavailable for family reasons. Quesada has still named a 33-man squad, recalling Ange Capuozzo for the first time since the Six Nations and calling up five uncapped players, including former Argentina international Domingo Miotti. Quesada says he has \"complete confidence in the players available.\""
