      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Pundit verdict",
          "heading": "Justin Marshall warns Scotland must not go insular against All Blacks",
          "body": "Justin Marshall, the former All Blacks scrum-half, tells Planet Rugby that Scotland must keep attacking against New Zealand this weekend. Last year Scotland came back from 17-0 down to 17-all before Damian McKenzie's cameo rescued the visitors. \"They went insular, started kicking the ball away,\" Marshall said, and Kieran Read adds that Scotland have too often lost the big games. Planet Rugby also points to wins over England, France and Argentina this year as proof of what Scotland can do."
        },
